					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1014468#post-2103269</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1014468/scp-4002-j#post-2103269</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 05 Sep 2014 16:17:50 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Zolgamax</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1707551</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>To be clear, the effect (making puns) is memetic, and the cheese wheel is sort of a &quot;host&quot; of the effect. Both interaction with the cheese wheel and interaction with someone whose speech is affected will cause a subject to start using puns in their speech.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1014468#post-2103085</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1014468/scp-4002-j#post-2103085</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 05 Sep 2014 10:06:38 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Crayne</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1346995</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>So viewing the cheese will make you start using cheese-related puns and those cheese-related puns will then go on to infect others, even if they haven't actually seen the cheese themselves? That's a bit of a muddled cognitohazard/memetic situation to be honest.</p> <p>Anyway, this didn't even make me smile. The amount of puns makes the article incredibly hard to read and the fact that many of them are pretty forced makes it even harder, sometimes making me wonder what the hell the original word was supposed to be.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
